# Line endings are the same on every machine: LF in the repository and LF in every checkout.
#
# git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true). Then a shell
# script copied into a Linux container fails on its first line ("/bin/sh^M"), Suricata reads its
# rules with a CR on the end, and the pinned hash of the vendored Swagger UI no longer matches.
# tests/test_portability.py checks the rules below. After pulling this file into an existing
# Windows checkout, run once:  git rm -r --cached . -q && git reset --hard
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF, which cmd.exe expects
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Byte-exact files: a vendored bundle whose SHA-256 is pinned, and log samples whose bytes are hashed
backend/static/swagger-ui/** -text
data/samples/** -text

# Binaries: never converted, never diffed as text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.parquet binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
